# Q29 (author, 2026-09-25: «одна ячейка там где объявление»; FABLE-OPUS-CODE-DATA-SPLIT-20260925-189
# c3c): the two bare assignments of the argument `arg` are ONE cell.  The first binds it (L3 §12), and
# the second writes the same cell -- a repeated bare assignment is not an occurrence, and `\[N]`
# numbers declarations.  So \[0]arg is 2.  (Until -189 they were two physical slots, 1 and 2.)
# \[1]arg has no second declaration to number: unit_occ_arg_second_refused.lm2.
fn: test (int: arg) int
    arg: 1
    arg: 2
    if: \[0]arg != 2
        return: 1
    return: 0
end: test
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: test(0); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
